 "unit_id": "CD1000-kinshasa-2",
 "as_of": "2026-10-01",
 "summary": "This unit covers most of Kinshasa's urban health-area neighbourhoods plus six villages of rural Maluku commune on the Plateau des Batéké. The city is firmly state-held: the PNC keeps order through commissariats and recurrent anti-Kuluna sweeps (Operation Ndobo), while Kuluna street gangs remain a serious but non-territorial criminal threat. Military camps (Camp Kokolo and adjacent garrison quarters, the naval base quarter) are run by the FARDC. In Maluku the FARDC (Operation Ngemba) is the main force against the Mobondo militia; after a DDR process launched in Dec 2025 the government claims pacification by mid-2026, but holdout Mobondo bands still attacked farms in May 2026, so these villages are FARDC-dominant with Mobondo raiding.",
